{"kind":"request","text":"claude: refiling the remote-link request on current bases. This replaces f696d5a9, which went stale under you; I am retiring it beside this filing, so answer this one and ignore that.\n\nNothing about the ask has changed and I checked rather than assuming. Hugh asked for this today: where we display the repository path, link it to the remote. I re-verified the premise at main 61439ecd — ui/src/components/TopBar.tsx lines 50-52 still render workroom.repo inside a plain span with a title attribute and no anchor. So the defect the original request described is exactly the defect that is there now, the conditions still describe work that needs doing, you are still the right addressee, and no decision under it has moved. The staleness was mine to clear, not a question for you.\n\nWhat did change is the ground beneath it. Main has moved twice since I filed the original — the ambient-Git hardening at c665af41 and the query sandbox at 7e88b9aa both landed — and the original's bases went with them. This one rests on the live internal/app artifact 30ec8051 at commit 61439ecd, which is the layer the remote has to come through, so the row should stay fresh while you work.\n\nI have carried the conditions across unchanged apart from naming the current TopBar lines. They were right when I wrote them and re-deriving them would only risk losing something. The security shape is the point of the exercise: an allowlist rather than a denylist, userinfo never reaching the DOM, and a mutation proof that the cross-site-scripting assertion actually fires when the allowlist is loosened. A green test that would stay green with a permissive check proves nothing here.\n\nThis is sequenced last and is not urgent. You have the narrow decision-records repair at 80af236d in front of it, and your spike and citation lanes in front of that. Promise it whenever you like; the promise records the owner, not a licence to start.","body":{"conditions":"Replaces stale request f696d5a9 with the same substance on current bases; premise re-verified at main 61439ecd. Not urgent, sequenced last behind your repair and spike lanes. The repository path shown in the workroom top bar links to the repository's remote URL when one exists and is safely linkable, and renders exactly as it does today when it is not. Carry the remote from git through app.LocalRepo and the /v0/worktrees response to the client type in ui/src/lib/api.ts and on to TopBar.tsx, where the plain span at lines 50-52 renders workroom.repo today. Only http and https URLs become an href, by allowlist and not by denylist; every other scheme, ssh and scp-style git@host:org/repo forms included, renders as today's plain text. Userinfo is removed from the rendered URL and from the href, or the link is declined when userinfo is present; state which you chose and why. If the link opens a new tab it carries rel=\"noopener noreferrer\". State which remote is used when a repository has several, and behave sanely with none. Regression tests written from the desired behaviour, not transcribed from current output, covering at least: an https remote links; an ssh or scp-style remote does not and falls back to plain text; a javascript: or data: scheme never reaches an href; a remote carrying userinfo does not leak it into the DOM; and no remote renders exactly as today. Prove mutation-sensitivity by replacing the scheme allowlist with a permissive check and watching the named cross-site-scripting assertion fail, then reverting. Rebuild the embedded bundle with make ui and keep make ui-check green in the same head, since the resident serves the committed embed rather than ui/src. Exact clean pushed head, per-path artifacts at every changed stable path including the two UI files which currently have none, gofmt, build, vet, npm test and go test ./... -count=1 green, independent review recording Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions. Do not merge.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f02491744